Show the keyboard type and secure entry TextInputConfiguration asks for on iOS.

What: gpui_ios's `keyboardType` reads `TextInputConfiguration::keyboard_type` through Flutter's `ToUIKeyboardType`
table (FlutterTextInputPlugin.mm @ 3.50.1: number → NumberPad, decimal → DecimalPad, phone → PhonePad, email →
EmailAddress, url → URL, search → WebSearch, text → Default), and a new `isSecureTextEntry` reads `secure`. Both were
missing: every field showed the default keyboard and no field was secure. The view already reloads its input views
when the configuration changes, so a field that turns secure or changes layout updates the keyboard.

Why: patch 0005 added the fields; this is the iOS backend reading them. Flutter tests (patch 0028's table)
testSecureInput, testKeyboardType, testKeyboardTypeWebSearch and testUpdateSecureTextEntry failed without it.

Test: patch 0028's rows, on the iOS simulator (`scripts/ios-text-oracle.sh` in Parallax).

Upstream PR: not filed yet (needs 0005 upstream first).

